$\Delta \mathrm{T}_{\mathrm{f}}=0.3^{\circ} \mathrm{C}$
$$
\begin{array}{l}
\Delta \mathrm{T}_{\mathrm{f}}=\frac{\mathrm{K}_{\mathrm{f}} \times \mathrm{W}_{\mathrm{B}} \times 1000}{\mathrm{M}_{\mathrm{B}} \times \mathrm{W}_{\mathrm{A}}} \\
0.3=\frac{1.86 \times \mathrm{W}_{\mathrm{B}} \times 1000}{62 \times 5000}
\end{array}
$$
$\therefore \mathrm{W}_{\mathrm{B}}=50 \mathrm{~g}$
The amount used should be more than $50 \mathrm{~g}$.
